  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A freeze this morning, then areas of frost tonight.\n\nTemperatures this morning have dropped to the coldest values for \nsome for this early winter season, with the lake plain under a \nfreeze warning where surface temperatures will approach 32F.\nWell inland areas are dropping down into the mid 20s.  \n\nBehind a surface ridge, a southwest flow will bring warming aloft, \nwith 850 hPa temperatures increasing into the upper single digits \nfor tonight. With a still clear sky and light wind areas of frost \nare likely to form, especially for areas outside of the northern \nNiagara Frontier that will lie closer to the center of the surface \nhigh. For the Niagara Frontier there may be enough of a gradient \nwind to limit the areal extent of the frost.  \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...An extended period of dry and warmer weather begins \nthis afternoon and likely lasts through the week.\n\nSurface high pressure will remain anchored over the eastern US this \nweek, that coupled with a ridge of high pressure aloft will maintain \nfair weather with afternoon temperatures near or above normal.",
